==Battleground==
*1 [[One Horn]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*1 [[Kid Tappa]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**1 [[Rain D.]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Rain D.|Rain Ds]] spawn after 1 second<sup>30f</sup>, delay 1~2 seconds<sup>30f~60f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 75% HP:
**1 [[Oldhorn]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Oldhorn]]s spawn after 1 second<sup>30f</sup>, delay 1~2 seconds<sup>30f~60f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 60% HP:
**1 [[Mr. Puffington]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Youcan]] spawns.
**1 [[Mr. Puffington]] spawns after 1 second<sup>30f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The Kid Tappa at the beginning can be used for stacking units such as [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]. When the One Horn makes it to the front line, it should be killed very quickly from the stack, allowing you to upgrade your Worker Cat. The first wave can be hard if not prepared, but luckily you can have a full wallet ready. Use [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic]] [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|meatshields]] and your choice of a unit to counter Rain D. It is not a problem to use [[:Category:Sniper-class Cats|Snipers]] against the Rain Ds because the high base health allows the Rain Ds to be defeated before the second wave is triggered. For the second wave, the Oldhorns have no support, so just stack DPS against them. The final wave can be dealt with a wave immune sniper and the Breakerblast Cannon. The Youcan misses often because of the Puffingtons, but be prepared for the boss shockwave.

==Trivia==
*Banishin' Tigers may be a reference to the [[wikipedia:Hanshin Tigers|Hanshin Tigers]], a Nippon Professional Baseball team playing in the Central League.
*The Japanese name of this stage is the first portion of the phrase "虎穴に入らずんば虎子を得ず" (''Koketsu ni Hairazunba Koji o Ezu''), meaning "You cannot gain anything without taking any risks".
*All enemies in this stage are males with the informal honorific くん ''-kun'' in their Japanese names ([[One Horn|Ikkaku-kun]], [[Kid Tappa|Manabu-kun]], [[Rain D.|Nakai-kun]], [[Oldhorn|Koraino-kun]], [[Mr. Puffington|Fuguta-kun]] and [[Youcan|Ōmu-kun]]). This honorific is primarily used with boys' names and between peers and friends.
**The only non-event ''-kuns'' excluded are [[The Face|Kaoru-kun]] and [[CyberFace|Metal Kaoru-kun]], possibly because their honorifics use the kanji 君 rather than kana.

